7. After considering the material placed before it and upon hearing the learned counsel for the parties, the NCLT noted that insofar as admission of the petition under Section 7 of the Code was concerned, it was necessary to ascertain whether there was a debt owed to the financial creditors;
whether there was a default with respect to such debt; and, as the financial creditors were allottees of a real estate project, to ascertain whether they fulfilled the threshold requirement stipulated by Section 7 of the Code so as to maintain their application.
8.
